    <h4 style="margin:16px 0 6px;">GPU passthrough (GPU-P / DDA / vGPU)</h4>
    <p class="muted" style="font-size:11px; margin:4px 0 8px;">Three ways a VM can get GPU acceleration. <strong>GPU-P</strong> is the active path on consumer Windows 11 hardware (uses Hyper-V GPU Partitioning, no extra license). <strong>DDA</strong> is fully wired — the driver rebind works on consumer SKUs but the VM-attach step needs a Windows Server license to actually succeed. <strong>NVIDIA vGPU</strong> needs an active vGPU license server. All destructive actions require explicit confirmation.</p>
    <div style="display:flex; gap:8px; margin-top:4px; align-items:center; flex-wrap:wrap;">
      <button type="button" id="settingsGpuPassRefresh" class="secondary">Refresh snapshot</button>
      <span id="settingsGpuPassStatus" class="muted" style="font-size:11px;"></span>
    </div>
    <div id="settingsGpuPassSnapshot" style="margin-top:8px; max-height:300px; overflow:auto; border:1px solid #2d2d44; border-radius:6px; padding:4px; background:#0e0f17; font-size:11px;">
