    </div>

    <details style="margin-top:10px;">
      <summary style="cursor:pointer; font-size:12px; color:#9999b4;">GPU-P fast path (create game-stream VM)</summary>
      <div style="margin-top:8px; padding:6px; border:1px solid #22243a; border-radius:6px;">
        <p class="muted" style="font-size:11px; margin:0 0 6px;">Provisions a Windows 11 VM via the <code>windows_game_stream_prebuilt</code> template. GPU-P partitioning is wired by HiveMind inside the template. Works on consumer Windows 11 + any modern NVIDIA GPU. Name must match <code>^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$</code>.</p>
        <div style="display:flex; gap:6px; align-items:center; flex-wrap:wrap;">
          <input id="settingsGpuPassVmName" type="text" placeholder="VM name (e.g. cyberpunk-stream-01)" style="flex:1; min-width:200px;">
          <button type="button" id="settingsGpuPassCreateVmBtn" class="secondary">Create GPU-P VM</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details style="margin-top:8px;">
      <summary style="cursor:pointer; font-size:12px; color:#9999b4;">DDA path (Hyper-V Discrete Device Assignment — wired for future WS license)</summary>
      <div style="margin-top:8px; padding:6px; border:1px solid #22243a; border-radius:6px;">
        <p class="muted" style="font-size:11px; margin:0 0 6px;">Rebinds a GPU to <code>vfio-pci</code> so a VM can claim it via DDA. <strong>Rebind works on consumer SKUs</strong>; the actual <code>Add-VMAssignableDevice</code> step needs Windows Server / Hyper-V Server. Use this once the license is acquired. <em>Destructive: dismounts the GPU from the host.</em></p>
